parametric-derivative.def:
For a curve $x = x(t)$, $y = y(t)$, the slope of the tangent line is $ rac{dy}{dx} =  rac{dy/dt}{dx/dt}$ wherever $ rac{dx}{dt} 
e 0$ (the chain rule solved for $ rac{dy}{dx}$). The tangent is horizontal where $ rac{dy}{dt} = 0$ and $ rac{dx}{dt} 
e 0$, and vertical where $ rac{dx}{dt} = 0$ and $ rac{dy}{dt} 
e 0$.
